DOS-PORT (patch 0095, Phase 9 wave 22 W22A). Decomposes the wave-20
W20B-measured mode_tick=23.94 ms median (91% of engine_tick) into 4
named sub-buckets + 1 derived residual. Single generic bracket-naming
scheme covers BOTH GM_NORMAL gameplay (game_tick_normal) AND title
attract (title_tick); bracket names describe work TYPE rather than
mode-specific terms so the same grep pattern reads across both
modes' samples.

Decomposes mode_tick because it is the dominant remaining engine-side
cost on real HW per W20B (docs/PHASE11-COLD-PICKUP.md § 1) and gates
wave-23+ optimization candidate selection. Wave-23 candidates ranked
in PHASE11-COLD-PICKUP.md § 4 (sprite cull / AI caching / skip-when-
unchanged / fixed-rate effects / drawcall batching / bullet pool) are
NOT pre-authored — per perf_predictions_unreliable.md and the wave-20
Levers C/D/E lesson (3 optimizations dropped on cross-validated
zero counters). Measure first; pick the dominant bucket; then act.

Implementation per docs/PHASE11-WAVE-22-CONTRACT.md (gitignored, on-
disk only):

1. **SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MODE_TICK_INSTR=1** env helper (strict-1, default
   OFF). NEW separate hint from W20B's FINE_INSTR per contract § 2 —
   preserves the strict-"1" convention from CLAUDE.md (rejecting
   numeric escalation `=2` on FINE_INSTR which would create an
   exception class) and keeps each instrumentation layer
   independently toggleable. Cached static-const-bool — -O2 hoists
   per-tick guards.

2. **4 RAII timer structs** in src/Utils/diagnostic_timers.h, mirroring
   W20B's ClearScreenTimer / TscInterpTimer / ModeTickTimer /
   DebugOverlayTimer pattern from patch 0090. Each gates on
   mode_tick_instr_active() at destruction; same construction-time
   SDL_GetTicksNS read as W20B (no constructor-side gate, consistent
   with EngineTickTimer + W20B precedent).

   - ModeSimTimer       — non-render game-state mutation
                          (HandlePlayer + AI + physics + scroll +
                           cull for GM_NORMAL; handle_input() for
                           title)
   - ModeDrawSceneTimer — primary scene drawcall pass
                          (DrawScene() for GM_NORMAL; draw_title()
                           for title — includes the in-OnTick
                           clearScreen on either mode)
   - ModeDrawHudTimer   — secondary HUD drawcalls
                          (StatusBar + fade + niku for GM_NORMAL;
                           empty for title — bracket fires n=0)
   - ModePostTimer      — post-render overlays + screen-effects
                          (textbox.Tick + ScreenEffects::Draw +
                           map_draw_map_name for GM_NORMAL;
                           textbox.Tick on the in_multiload-and-
                           SaveSelect-visible branch for title)

3. **Storage** (file-scope in Renderer.cpp's NXE::Diag namespace,
   alongside W20B's storage so audit-flush emits 3 layers from a
   single TU):
   - 4 sample arrays + 4 idx counters
   - 1 residual sample array + 1 residual idx
   - 4 per-tick dt locals (reset at Game::tick entry; written by
     each timer's destructor; consumed by the residual block)

   Reuses W20B's g_eng_tick_block_size = 100 (per contract § 3 — no
   new block_size constant introduced).

4. **Residual derivation** (option α from contract § 4) at end of
   Game::tick body, gated separately from W20B's residual block.
   Reuses W20B's g_eng_mode_tick_dt_this_tick (populated by
   ModeTickTimer in patch 0090) as the parent total — NO new
   SDL_GetTicksNS read at end-of-tick because W20B already captures
   the dispatch-call delta.

       _mt_residual = g_eng_mode_tick_dt_this_tick
                    - mode_sim_dt - mode_draw_scene_dt
                    - mode_draw_hud_dt - mode_post_dt

   Signed math + clamp at 0. Self-validating: small mode_residual
   median (<1 ms) means brackets are exhaustive for that scene;
   large residual surfaces an unbracketed chunk.

   IMPORTANT: this is residual within mode_tick, NOT residual within
   engine_tick. W20B's engine_tick_residual block continues to tell
   you what's in Game::tick body OUTSIDE tickfunctions[].OnTick().
   Both layers stay independently meaningful.

   COUPLING: the W22A residual block reads g_eng_mode_tick_dt_this_-
   tick which is only written when FINE_INSTR=1. With MODE_TICK_INSTR=1
   but FINE_INSTR=0, residual silently clamps to 0 every tick (sub-
   bucket samples remain valid). Operator's W22A iter (contract § 6)
   sets both hints, so this is not a real-world issue; documented
   in BOOT.md (on-disk only).

5. **Audit-flush emission** in _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit() in
   Renderer.cpp: 5 new

       [mode-tick-stat n=N phase=<NAME> min=N.NN med=N.NN mean=N.NN
        p95=N.NN max=N.NN ms]

   lines per 100-tick block when MODE_TICK_INSTR=1. Distinct prefix
   `mode-tick-stat` (vs W20A's `flip-stat` and W20B's
   `engine-tick-stat`) so 3-layer grep tooling separates the layers
   without ambiguity. Empty-block placeholder lines (n=0, all
   numerics 0.00) emitted for buckets with zero firings so per-block
   log shape stays uniform — critical for W22A1 (title) where
   mode_draw_hud always fires n=0 and the title common branch fires
   mode_post n=0. Analysis tooling expects 5 lines per block.

   Order in the log per block: [flip-stat] (W20A) → [engine-tick-stat]
   (W20B) → [mode-tick-stat] (W22A) → counters. Outer-to-inner
   decomposition; greppable in priority order.

6. **Same _compute_flip_phase_stats helper** reused (W20A's
   sort/min/med/mean/p95/max/2-decimal infrastructure is layer-
   agnostic; same _FlipPhaseStats struct). NO fourth-layer copy of
   the helper introduced — three copies would diverge over time.

7. **Cross-namespace plumbing** mirrors W20B precedent: forward-
   declared free function NXE::Diag::mode_tick_instr_active() at
   namespace scope (alongside engine_tick_fine_instr_active() in the
   file-top wrapper) with a 1-line definition at file scope after
   BOTH outer NXE::Graphics namespace braces close. Heeds the W20B
   build-fix amendment — placement at "after the anonymous namespace
   closes but BEFORE the outer NXE::Graphics closes" would re-open
   NXE inside NXE::Graphics, producing nested NXE::Graphics::NXE::Diag.
   File-scope placement after-both-namespace-closes is correct;
   same trap, same fix.

Bracket-placement decisions vs contract § 1 (transparent flag of
contract-text-vs-implementation deltas, per silent-narrow rule —
all 3 acked by flush-instr at Task #3 review):

a. game_tick_normal()'s 2 player-init lines (player->riding = NULL;
   player->bopped_object = NULL) at game.cpp:345-346 fall into
   mode_residual rather than mode_sim. Contract § 1 enumerated
   "lines 347-371" (UpdateBlockStates onwards) for mode_sim;
   the 2 NULL-writes weren't in scope. Sub-µs work; residual
   absorbs without distorting headlines.

b. title_tick()'s seldelay-branch clearScreen + in_multiload-non-
   textbox-branch clearScreen fall into mode_residual rather than
   mode_post. Contract § 1 said "the clearScreen(BLACK) at
   title.cpp:346 / 360 (inside the bracket, since these are post-
   input frames)" but those clearScreens are on alternative control-
   flow branches that don't visit the textbox.Tick() call site at
   all — wrapping them with mode_post would be artificial. Drop to
   residual is the cleaner code-faithful reading. Per pressure_-
   test_tidy_narratives.md the contract over-prescribed; flush-instr
   acked the placement at review.

c. mode_draw_hud (375-380) placed before mode_post (382-385) in
   game_tick_normal() — matches contract § 1 left-to-right
   enumeration.

Non-coverage (intentional, per contract § 1):
- audio_mix_stage NOT bracketed as a sibling — Pixtone/Organya
  output staging fires off-thread in audio-IRQ context (no clean
  call site inside OnTick body). Audio-IRQ wall-clock cost continues
  to be captured by the audio-on vs audio-off engine_tick_total
  delta from W20B + W20A2.
- Per-OnTick clearScreen INSIDE the mode_draw_scene bracket, NOT
  separate. The W20B ClearScreenTimer brackets the OUTER Game::tick-
  level clearScreen at game.cpp:254; per-mode clearScreens are
  different call sites and separate work.
- Non-load-bearing modes (inventory_tick, ms_tick, island_tick,
  credit_tick, intro_tick, pause_tick, options_tick, mods_tick) get
  NO instrumentation. Operator's W22A iter doesn't enter them in
  measured frames. Brackets add cleanly later if a future scene
  surfaces a need.

Hot-path cost when MODE_TICK_INSTR unset (mirrors W20B):
- 4 RAII destructors per OnTick (each reads SDL_GetTicksNS at
  construction unconditionally; gating happens at destruction)
- ~5 KB unused static state (5 sample arrays × 100 × sizeof(uint64)
  + 4 dt locals + 5 idxes)
- Residual block: gated on mode_tick_instr_active(), 0 cost when
  env unset

Documentation: docs/BOOT.md gets a comprehensive MODE_TICK_INSTR
entry covering bracket scheme, residual semantics, empty-block
placeholder behavior, FINE_INSTR pairing dependency, and the
strict-match convention. BOOT.md is gitignored per pre-existing
convention (.gitignore:95) — internal-only docs that live on-disk
for reference, not in the public repo. Same situation as W20B's
FINE_INSTR doc gap (flagged by flush-instr's W22A side-observation).

